  "sections": {
    "BASICS": {
      "present": true,
      "status": "content",
      "content_blocks": [],
      "subsections": {
        "OVERVIEW": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "OVERVIEW",
          "canonical_heading": "OVERVIEW",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Flies of the genusCuterebraare found in the Americas, where they are obligatory parasites of rodents and lagomorphs. Adult flies lay eggs on blades of grass or in nests; they hatch and crawl onto the skin of passing host. The small maggots enter a body orifice, migrate through various internal tissues, and ultimately over several weeks to months make their way to the skin, where they establish a warble. The mature maggots, which may be an inch long, then drop out of the rodent or rabbit host and pupate in the soil.",
              "pdf_page": 433,
              "printed_page": 351,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Dogs and cats become infected when they contact a blade of grass upon which an egg containing an infective maggot is stimulated to hatch and attach onto the passing animal. The maggots then crawl around on the cat or dog until they find an orifice in which to enter.",
              "pdf_page": 433,
              "printed_page": 351,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Dogs and cats can develop maggots in warbles or can develop signs associated with larvae migrating within their tissues.",
              "pdf_page": 433,
              "printed_page": 351,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Dogs and cats can present with respiratory signs, neurologic signs, ophthalmic lesions, or maggots in their skin.",
              "pdf_page": 433,
              "printed_page": 351,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
